chunk\n- `markdown_renderer.format_text` for small initial text\n- String processing for role prefix, separator, etc.\n\n### 6. Every 10 chunks: full session serialization\n- `vim.json.encode` for the session with growing message\n\n---\n\nNow let me propose concrete fixes:\n\n### Fix 1: Throttle `apply_highlights` - only highlight the delta region\n\nInstead of highlighting from `message_start_line` to end, only highlight the newly added\/modified lines. The previous lines already have correct highlights.\n\nFor the incremental path, we know exactly which lines changed:\n- If delta has no newlines: only 1 line changed (last_content_line)\n- If delta has newlines: lines from last_content_line to last_content_line + #delta_parts\n\nSo we can either:\na) Call `apply_highlights` with a limited end_line\nb) Only call highlights when content \"settles\" (e.g., no new content for 50ms)\n\n### Fix 2: Debounce `apply_highlights` across chunks\n\nInstead of calling `apply_highlights` on every chunk via `vim.schedule`, use a debounce timer (like 50ms) so that rapid...[truncated]
